            "datePublished": "29 Mar 2024 00:00:00 GMT",
            "about": "Island was originally recorded at Studio Syrland and Hot Ice, Iceland between 1986-1991.\nIsland features David Tibet - vocals; HÖH: keyboards, acoustic guitar, bass, guitar, harp, percussion; Björk Gudmundsdóttir - backing vocals on Falling; Akiko Hada - backing vocals on Falling; Thór Eldon - guitar; Godkrist - guitar on Passing Horses; Liz Aster - backing vocals on Fields Of Rape and Merry-Go-Round; Bogomil Font - backing vocals on Merry-Go-Round; Ása Hlín Svavarsdóttir - vocals on The Dream Of A Shadow Of Smoke; The Venerable `Chimed Rig'dzin Lama, Rinpoche - bells and drums on Anyway, People Die; Johnny Triumph - backing vocals on Merry-Go-Round; Joolie Wood - violin on Anyway, People Die and Merry-Go-Round; Tómas M. Tómasson - bass guitar on The Dream Of A Shadow Of Smoke and To Blackened Earth.\nTrack Listing:\nA1 - Falling\nA2 - The Dream Of A Shadow Of Smoke\nA3 - Lament For My Suzanne\nA4 - Fields Of Rape (Sightless Return)\nB1 - Passing Horses\nB2 - Anyway, People Die\nB3 - To Blackened Earth\nB4 - Oh Merry-Go-Round\nRemastered by The Bricoleur",
